---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import ArrowLink from '../components/ArrowLink.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { MEDIA } from '../content/media';
import { SITE } from '../content/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Pierce O’Brien | Pierce O’Brien Piano"
  description="Meet Pierce O’Brien and learn about the careful listening, assessment, and plain-language guidance behind his piano work."
>
  <PageIntro
    title="About Pierce"
    introduction="Pierce O’Brien, RPT, is a guild-certified piano technician who treats tuning as a relationship between the piano, the player, and the room."
    image={MEDIA.portrait}
    imageAlt="Portrait of Pierce O’Brien seated in front of a grand piano"
    imagePosition="center 28%"
    actionLabel="Book With Pierce"
  />

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="portrait-layout shell">
      <div class="media-frame">
        <Image
          src={MEDIA.workingMonochrome}
          alt="Pierce O’Brien working at the open strings of a grand piano"
          widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 40vw"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>A trained ear, shaped in demanding rooms.</h2>
        <p>
          Before moving to Salt Lake City, Pierce spent more than five years in Nashville’s
          recording industry. The work put him around exacting performers, songwriters, and sessions
          where the smallest detail could change the sound in the room.
        </p>
        <p>
          That background still guides his piano work: listen closely, understand the instrument in
          front of you, and explain what matters without leaving an owner out of the conversation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pierce tunes by ear. His approach respects the way each piano responds differently,
          looking beyond pitch alone to the touch, tone, condition, and character that make an
          instrument feel like itself.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every appointment begins with an assessment and consultation. At the first appointment,
          Pierce also includes light dusting and key cleaning, then gives practical recommendations
          for the care that will help the piano stay ready to play.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>A method built around the piano in front of you.</h2>
        <p>
          The goal is not a one-size-fits-all result. It is a piano that sounds and feels more at
          home with the person playing it, plus a clear plan for the care ahead.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="process-rail">
        <section class="process-step">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Listen</h3>
          <p>Start with what the owner hears, feels, and hopes the piano can do.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="process-step">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Tune by ear</h3>
          <p>Work with the piano’s pitch, touch, tone, and individual character.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="process-step">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Plan for care</h3>
          <p>Leave with useful recommendations for follow-up care and a better-kept piano.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="owner-event shell">
      <div class="owner-event-copy">
        <h2>Continued study, close to the work.</h2>
        <p>
          This owner-supplied photograph records Pierce at the 2026 Piano Technicians Guild
          convention. Continued study keeps the work grounded in careful listening, thoughtful
          assessment, and better choices for each individual instrument.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="owner-event-photo">
        <Image
          src={MEDIA.rptEvent}
          alt="Pierce O’Brien beside an event display at a piano-technician convention"
          widths={[420, 720, 1080, 1400]}
          sizes="(max-width: 960px) 86vw, 42vw"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>Owner-supplied convention photograph.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark statement">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="statement-copy">
        The value of a piano is not limited to its price. A family’s first upright deserves the same
        honest attention as a performance grand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="closing-action shell">
      <h2>Work directly with the technician.</h2>
      <ArrowLink href={SITE.booking.internalPath} label="Book Now" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
